From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:26:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/25] REIMS_VGPU_PAGED_BUFFER_CACHE keeps
 paged textures' buffers

Safari's compositor makes a texture per rAF on a dozen recycled page ranges.
Each cost about 148 mmaps, a Vulkan import, a free and munmaps on the exec's
serial path, 53% of the busy task thread. Off by default. A hit needs the
pages the task maps now: every lookup walks the guest's page table.

Also: mapstat per present, a log line per 600 presents, tdesc and srf events.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
